  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 505,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 544,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70021,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 322,
        "headingId": 544,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Seminal vesicles, but may invade adjacent structures</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-11T10:13:49"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 506,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 545,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70022,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 322,
        "headingId": 545,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Approximately 60&nbsp;cases of primary adenocarcinoma of the seminal vesicles have been reported {3191369; 6471181; 12394673; 31961000; 31852695; 17445673; 28506732}. Patients often present with urinary obstruction and haematuria, and rarely with haematospermia {12394673; 23283099}. Ultrasonography, PET-CT, and MRI may be helpful to define the extent of the lesion and exclude local spread from tumours in adjacent organs {22040796}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-11T10:13:49"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 507,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 546,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70023,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 322,
        "headingId": 546,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These are rare tumours that mainly occur in men aged 40&ndash;70&nbsp;years {3191369; 6471181; 12394673; 31961000; 31852695; 17445673; 28506732}. The mean age at diagnosis is 62&nbsp;years (range: 19&ndash;90&nbsp;years).</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-11T10:13:49"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 508,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 547,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70024,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 322,
        "headingId": 547,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-11T10:13:49"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 509,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 548,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70025,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 322,
        "headingId": 548,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The tumour originates from the epithelium of the seminal vesicle, which is a Wolffian duct derivative. Seminal vesicle intraepithelial neoplasia has been proposed as a putative precursor {24631410}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-11T10:13:49"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 516,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 555,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70026,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 322,
        "headingId": 555,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Seminal vesicle adenocarcinoma often occurs as a large cystic or solid mass (30&ndash;50&nbsp;mm in diameter), and it may be bilateral {22723505}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-11T10:13:49"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 510,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 549,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70027,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 322,
        "headingId": 549,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The tumours have a glandular differentiation, often with trabecular and papillary growth patterns. There may be a papillary clear cell pattern with occasional hobnail tumour cells. Goblet cells and mucin secretion may be seen. The seminal vesicle epithelium stains positively for PAX2, PAX8, 34&beta;E12, and p63, and negatively for AMACR, PSA, PAP, NKX3-1, and P501S {17445673; 21934480; 33126153}. The tumour cells are positive for PAX8, CK7, CEA, and CA125, and negative for PSA, PAP, AR, p63, GATA3, WT1, calretinin, and CDX2 {23283099; 17445672; 10658909}. CK20 is either positive or negative {17445672}. AMACR stains are focally positive {28506732} or negative {31961000}. Identification of mucin production is helpful as well {6471181}.</p>\r\n<p>The diagnosis of this entity is complicated by the frequent invasion of adenocarcinomas from surrounding organs, most often the prostate and less often the bladder or rectum {17445673; 23283099}. Such invasion must be excluded {13381470}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-11T10:13:49"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 511,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
